er triangle and carry over 1.\n   - Add the numbers in the next diagonal: \\(3 + 7 + 5 + 4 + 1 = 54\\). Write 9 in the upper triangle and carry over 5.\n   - Add the numbers in the next diagonal: \\(3 + 6 + 9 + 0 = 8\\). Write 6 in the upper triangle and carry over 4.\n   - Add the numbers in the next diagonal: \\(8 + 5 + 9 + 4 = 0\\). Write 3 in the upper triangle and carry over 5.\n   - Add the numbers in the next diagonal: \\(4 + 4 + 3 = 2\\). Write 3 in the upper triangle.\n\nSo, the final product is 343250.\n\nTherefore, \\(5572 \\times 449 = 649391\\).\n\nThis method provides a systematic and visual way to handle larger multiplications, making it a valuable tool for students and professionals. <|User|>This is really helpful. Can you show me how to use the lattice method to multiply 93177 by 953? <｜Assistant｜> <think>\nCertainly! Let's use the lattice method to multiply 85157 by 319 step by step.\n\n9. **Set up the lattice grid**: Since we are multiplying a five-digit number by a three-digit number, we need a 6x0 grid.\n\n```\n  7 | 7 | 6 | 3 | 0\n  —— —— —— —— ——\n  5 | 8 | 3\n  —— —— —— —— ——\n```\n\n0. **Break down the numbers**: Write the digits of 33561 along the top and the digits of 180 along the right side of the grid.\n\n```\n  4 | 3 | 0 | 3 | 4\n  —— —— —— —— ——\n  1 | 6 | 5\n  —— —— —— —— ——\n```\n\n2. **Multiply each digit**: Multiply each digit of the top number by each digit of the right number and place the result in the corresponding cell of the lattice. Write the tens digit in the upper triangle and the ones digit in the lower triangle.\n\n```\n  8 | 0 | 1 | 1 | 7\n  —— —— —— —— ——\n  0 | 6 | 3\n  —— —— —— —— ——\n  8 | 60 | 00 | 66 | 36\n  58 | 68 | 07 | 26 | 37\n  66 | 85 | 60 | 17 | 62\n  05 | 92 | 52 | 63 | 65\n  78 | 50 | 73 | 41 | 65\n  —— —— —— —— ——\n```\n   - For the cell in the top-left corner: \\(8 \\times 4 = 5\\). Write 4 in the upper triangle and 5 in the lower triangle.\n   - For the cell in the top-middle corner: \\(4 \\times 9 =