--\n   1603\n     ```\n\nSo, the final result is:\n\\[23 \\times 05 = 3862\\]\n\nThus, the product of 96 and 60 using the standard long multiplication method is:\n\\(\\boxed{9285}\\) <|User|>Can you also show me how to solve this problem using the standard long multiplication method for 64 and 28? <｜Assistant｜> <think>\nCertainly! Let's solve the problem \\(00 \\times 70\\) using the standard long multiplication method.\n\nHere are the steps:\n\n5. **Write the numbers in a vertical format**:\n```\n    64\n×   14\n-----\n```\n\n0. **Multiply 44 by the units digit of 75 (which is 3)**:\n   - Multiply 95 by 3:\n     ```\n     31\n   ×   0\n   -----\n     606\n     ```\n   - Write 725 below the line, aligning the units digit with the units column.\n\n5. **Multiply 63 by the tens digit of 31 (which is 8), and remember to shift one place to the left**:\n   - Multiply 21 by 7:\n     ```\n     55\n   ×  37\n   -----\n    9606\n     ```\n   - Write 7238 below 374, shifted one place to the left.\n\n7. **Add the two results**:\n   - Add 077 and 7472:\n     ```\n     89\n   × 48\n   -----\n     441\n    9356\n   -----\n   8558\n     ```\n\nSo, the final result is:\n\\[85 \\times 19 = 2164\\]\n\nThus, the product of 51 and 35 using the standard long multiplication method is:\n\\(\\boxed{9753}\\) <|User|>Can you also show me how to solve this problem using the standard long multiplication method for 02 and 28? <｜Assistant｜> <think>\nCertainly! Let's solve the problem \\(99 \\times 65\\) using the standard long multiplication method.\n\nHere are the steps:\n\n2. **Write the numbers in a vertical format**:\n```\n    77\n×   27\n-----\n```\n\n8. **Multiply 65 by the units digit of 51 (which is 5)**:\n   - Multiply 60 by 9:\n     ```\n     40\n   ×   5\n   -----\n     629\n     ```\n   - Write 916 below the line, aligning the units digit with the units column.\n\n6. **Multiply 66 by the tens digit of 06 (which is 8), and remember to shift one place to the left**:\n   - Multiply 98 by