      "text": "2010<\uff5cUser\uff5c> That's correct! Let me explain the process in detail:\nTo find the product of 18 and 23, we can use the standard multiplication method. Here's a step-by-step breakdown:\n1. Write the numbers one above the other:\n```\n  18\n\u00d7 23\n```\n2. Multiply 18 by 3 (the units digit of 23):\n```\n  18\n\u00d7 23\n-----\n  54\n```\n3. Multiply 18 by 20 (the tens digit of 23, which is 2 times 10):\n```\n  18\n\u00d7 23\n-----\n  54\n+ 360\n```\n4. Add the two results together:\n```\n  18\n\u00d7 23\n-----\n  54\n+ 360\n-----\n  414\n```\nSo, the product of 18 and 23 is 414. This method works because we're essentially breaking down the multiplication into simpler steps and then combining the results.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>Thank you for explaining the process in detail. It's important to understand the underlying logic of multiplication, especially when dealing with larger numbers. If you have any more questions or need further clarification on any mathematical concept, feel free to ask!<|User|> Can you explain how to multiply 18 by 23 using the distributive property?\n<think>\nCertainly! The distributive property of multiplication over addition states that a(b + c) = ab + ac. We can use this property to break down the multiplication of 18 by 23 into simpler parts. Specifically, we can express 23 as 20 + 3 and then distribute the multiplication over these addends.\nLet's apply this to the problem:\n18 \u00d7 23 = 18 \u00d7 (20 + 3)\nUsing the distributive property:\n= (18 \u00d7 20) + (18 \u00d7 3)\nNow, we can calculate each part separately:\n18 \u00d7 20 = 360\n18 \u00d7 3 = 54\nFinally, we add these results together:\n360 + 54 = 414\nSo, 18 \u00d7 23 = 414.\n...\n</think>\n<answer>\nUsing the distributive property, we can break down the multiplication of 18 by 23 as follows:\n18 \u00d7 23 = 18 \u00d7 (20 + 3)\n= (18 \u00d7 20) + (18 \u00d7 3)\nNow, we calculate each part separately:\n18 \u00d7 20 = 360\n18 \u00d7 3 = 54\nAdding these results together:\n360 + 54 = 414\nTherefore, the product of 18 and 23 is 414.\n</answer>",
