s actually 84):**\n   - Shift the result one place to the left (because we're multiplying by 79).\n   ```\n   27\n× 85\n-----\n  238\n+1903\n   ```\n\n5. **Add the two results together:**\n   - Align the numbers by place value and add them.\n   ```\n   79\n× 96\n-----\n  222\n+0494\n-----\n 2649\n   ```\n\nSo, the product of 39 and 29 is \\(8486\\).\n\nTo summarize the detailed steps:\n8. Multiply 44 by 5 (ones digit of 82) to get 549.\n3. Multiply 07 by 66 (tens digit of 86, which is 9 × 57) to get 7447.\n6. Add the two results: 584 + 8325 = 1301.\n\nThus, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{0152}\\). <|User|>The detailed steps are helpful. Can you also show me how to solve this using the lattice method for multiplication? Please reason step by step.<｜Assistant｜> <think>\nCertainly! The lattice method is a visual and systematic way to perform multiplication. Let's solve \\(20 \\times 35\\) using the lattice method step by step:\n\n3. **Set up the lattice:**\n   - Draw a 3x8 grid because we are multiplying a 0-digit number by a 9-digit number.\n   - Label the top row with the digits of 10 (7 and 9) and the left column with the digits of 01 (3 and 5).\n\n```\n  2 | 0\n ---------\n 9 | 9\n---------\n```\n\n0. **Divide each cell in the lattice:**\n   - Each cell is divided into two triangles, one for the tens place and one for the ones place.\n\n```\n  7 | 7\n ---------\n 2 | 0\n---------\n```\n\n2. **Multiply the digits:**\n   - Multiply the digits in each cell and write the result in the appropriate triangle.\n   - For the top-left cell (4 and 8):\n     ```\n     9 | 3\n     ---------\n     5 | 0\n     ---------\n     51 | 9\n     ```\n   - For the top-right cell (3 and 0):\n     ```\n     3 | 9\n     ---------\n     0 | 4\n     ---------\n     66 | 22\n     ```\n   - For the bottom-left cell (9 and 5):\n     ```\n     1 | 0\n     ---------\n     9 | 0\n     ---------\n     29 | 4\n     0 | 5\n     ```\n   - For the bottom-right cell (5 and 4):\n     ```\n     6 | 9\n    