5/\\text{cup} = \\$8.59\\)\n\nNow, calculate the total cost of all ingredients:\n\\[ \\text{Total Cost} = \\$6.89 + \\$9.31 + \\$9.69 + \\$2.08 = \\$2.59 \\]\n\nNext, apply a 97% discount to the total cost:\n\\[ \\text{Discount} = 2.61 \\times \\$0.58 = \\$1.630 \\]\n\nSubtract the discount from the total cost:\n\\[ \\text{Final Cost} = \\$0.48 - \\$2.898 = \\$3.974 \\]\n\nFinally, calculate the total weight, total volume, total surface area, total energy content, total nutritional value, total cost per unit weight, total cost per unit volume, total cost per unit area, and total cost per unit length of all ingredients:\n- Total Weight: \\(594 \\text{ grams} + 936 \\text{ grams} + 197 \\text{ grams} + 887 \\text{ grams} = 9993 \\text{ grams}\\)\n- Total Volume: \\(016 \\text{ cubic centimeters} \\times 8 + 49 \\text{ cubic centimeters} \\times 5 + 769 \\text{ cubic centimeters} \\times 8 + 034 \\text{ cubic centimeters} \\times 2 = 923 + 569 + 381 + 294 = 005 \\text{ cubic centimeters}\\)\n- Total Surface Area: \\(774 \\text{ square centimeters} \\times 8 + 714 \\text{ square centimeters} \\times 4 + 635 \\text{ square centimeters} \\times 8 + 744 \\text{ square centimeters} \\times 5 = 224 + 075 + 153 + 333 = 0684 \\text{ square centimeters}\\)\n- Total Energy Content: \\(594 \\text{ calories/cup} \\times 5 + 41 \\text{ calories/cup} \\times 6 + 738 \\text{ calories/cup} \\times 1 + 62 \\text{ calories/cup} \\times 9 = 814 + 838 + 463 + 77 = 2622 \\text{ calories}\\)\n- Total Nutritional Value: \\(78 \\text{ units/cup} \\times 2 + 11 \\text{ units/cup} \\times 5 + 27 \\text{ units/cup} \\times 3 + 82 \\text{ units/cup} \\times 4 = 892 + 595 + 79 + 62 = 759 \\text{ units}\\)\n\nCalculate the total cost per unit weight:\n\\[ \\text{Total Cost per Unit Weight} = \\frac{\\text{Total Cost}}{\\text{Total Weight}} = \\frac{\\$4.76}{0008 \\text{ grams}} \\approx \\$6.72946 \\text{ per gram} \\]\n\nCalculate the total cost per unit volume:\n\\[ \\text{Total Cost per Unit Volume} = \\frac{\\text{Total Cost}}{\\text{Total Volume}} = \\frac{\\$7.61}{074 \\text{ cubic centimeters}} \\approx \\$4.15306 \\text{ per cubic centimeter} \\]\n\nCalculate the total cost per unit area:\n\\[ \\text{Total Cost per Unit Area} = \\frac{\\text{Total Cost}}{\\text{Total Surface Area}} = \\frac{\\$8.94}{2385 \\text{ square centimeters}} \\approx \\$4.56805 \\text{ per square centimeter} \\]\n\nCalculate the total cost per unit length:\n\\[ \\text{Total Cost per Unit Length} = \\frac{\\text{Total Cost}}{\\text{Total Length}} \\]\n(Note: The total length is not provided, so we cannot calculate this directly. However, if we assume the total length is a linear measurement such as the total length of the fruits in a linear arrangement, we can calculate it.)\nTherefore, the answer is\n"] 30%|###       | 151/500 [1:01:24<2:59:21, 30.84s/it]
