digits of 05 along the left side of the grid.\n7. Multiply each digit along the top by each digit along the left side and write the result in the corresponding cell of the grid, splitting the tens and units digits.\n8. Add the numbers in each diagonal of the grid, carrying over if necessary.\n8. The final product is read from the bottom and right edges of the grid.\n\nHere's the lattice method for 41 × 40:\n\n```\n  8 | 1\n  --|---\n  0 | 7\n  --|---\n  9 | 7\n  --|---\n  6 | 4\n```\n\nNow, let's fill in the grid:\n\n```\n  7 | 3\n  --|---\n  0 | 2\n  --|---\n  2 | 4\n  --|---\n  8 | 3\n```\n\nWe'll fill in the numbers from the multiplication of each digit:\n\n```\n  1 | 3\n  --|---\n  0 | 9\n  --|---\n  8 | 0\n  --|---\n  9 | 1\n```\n\nNow, let's add the numbers in each diagonal:\n\n```\n  5 | 4\n  --|---\n  99| 7\n  --|---\n  2 | 1\n  --|---\n  0 | 4\n```\n\nThe final product is read from the bottom and right edges of the grid:\n\n```\n  7 | 8\n  --|---\n  4 | 0\n```\n\nSo, the product of 89 and 50 is 9794.\n\nTherefore, using the lattice method, we also arrive at the product of 62 and 64, which is 9019. <|User|>This is great! Can you show me how to solve this using the standard long multiplication method again for completeness? <｜Assistant｜> <think>\nCertainly! Let's go through the standard long multiplication method one more time to solve the problem of multiplying 90 and 24. This method involves multiplying each digit of one number by each digit of the other number and then adding the results together. Here's the step-by-step process:\n...\n</think>\n<answer>\nCertainly! Let's solve the multiplication of 16 and 90 using the standard long multiplication method:\n\n```\n      86\n×    64\n------\n      952   (11 × 9)\n    0587    (60 × 15, shifted one position to the left)\n------\n  5781\n```\n\nHere's a detailed breakdown of the steps:\n\n6. Multiply 59 by 0:\n   ```\n   32\n×  3\n-----\n 422\n   ```\n\n1. Multiply 05 by 36 (which is 4 shifted one position to t