      "text": "8458. However, this approach seems to be incorrect as it doesn't align with the problem statement. Let's use the straightforward multiplication method instead.\n</think>\n<answer>\nTo find the product of 79 and 80, we can use the distributive property of multiplication over addition. We can express 80 as 80 = 80, and then use the distributive property:\n\\[ 79 \\times 80 = 79 \\times (80) = 79 \\times (8 \\times 10) = (79 \\times 8) \\times 10 \\]\n\nFirst, let's calculate \\( 79 \\times 8 \\):\n\\[ 79 \\times 8 = (80 - 1) \\times 8 = 80 \\times 8 - 1 \\times 8 = 640 - 8 = 632 \\]\n\nNow, we multiply the result by 10:\n\\[ 632 \\times 10 = 6320 \\]\n\nTherefore, the product of 79 and 80 is:\n\\[ \\boxed{6320} \\]\n</answer>",
