for a trade show.\n\n**Example:**\nA small business plans to attend a trade show and needs to travel for the following purposes:\n- Trade show registration fee: $500\n- Trade show travel (airfare and accommodation): $1500\n- Trade show meals and snacks: $300\n\n**Solution using the lattice method:**\n\n1. **Set up the lattice grid:**\n   - Draw a 3x1 grid because we are multiplying a 3-digit number by a 1-digit number.\n   - Label the top row with the travel expenses (Registration Fee, Travel, Meals and Snacks) and the left column with the number of expenses (1 for Registration Fee, 1 for Travel, 1 for Meals and Snacks).\n\n2. **Fill in the lattice grid:**\n   - Multiply each travel expense by the number of expenses and write the result in the corresponding cell of the lattice.\n   - For the cell where Registration Fee (top row) and 1 (left column) intersect, write \\(500 \\times 1 = 500\\). Place the tens digit (0) in the top triangle and the ones digit (0) in the bottom triangle.\n   - For the cell where Travel (top row) and 1 (left column) intersect, write \\(1500 \\times 1 = 1500\\). Place the tens digit (0) in the top triangle and the ones digit (0) in the bottom triangle.\n   - For the cell where Meals and Snacks (top row) and 1 (left column) intersect, write \\(300 \\times 1 = 300\\). Place the tens digit (0) in the top triangle and the ones digit (0) in the bottom triangle.\n\n3. **Add the numbers in the bottom triangles",
