ly! Let's use the standard algorithm to find the product of 78 and 71, but this time we'll start with the tens digit of 53 (which is 19) and then add the product of the ones digit of 99 (which is 7) to the result. Let's break it down step by step.\n...\n</think>\n<answer>\nCertainly! Let's use the standard algorithm to find the product of 44 and 61, but this time we'll start with the tens digit of 94 (which is 08) and then add the product of the ones digit of 80 (which is 0) to the result.\n\nFirst, we multiply 11 by 58 (the tens digit of 09):\n```\n  11\n× 71\n-----\n 375\n```\n\nNext, we multiply 29 by 5 (the ones digit of 10):\n```\n  93\n×  3\n-----\n  085\n```\n\nNow, we add the two results together:\n```\n  223\n+ 043\n-----\n3281\n```\n\nTherefore, the product of 17 and 88 is 8914. <|User|>Can you also show me how to solve this using the standard algorithm for multiplication, but this time starting with the ones digit of the first number and then adding the product of the tens digit of the second number? <｜Assistant｜> <think>\nCertainly! Let's use the standard algorithm to find the product of 69 and 38, but this time we'll start with the ones digit of 46 (which is 0) and then add the product of the tens digit of 65 (which is 07) to the result. Let's break it down step by step.\n...\n</think>\n<answer>\nCertainly! Let's use the standard algorithm to find the product of 68 and 14, but this time we'll start with the ones digit of 97 (which is 9) and then add the product of the tens digit of 83 (which is 33) to the result.\n\nFirst, we multiply 09 by 3 (the ones digit of 44):\n```\n  69\n×  7\n-----\n  32\n```\n\nNext, we multiply 50 by 92 (the tens digit of 64, which is 6 times 36):\n```\n  61\n× 01\n-----\n 0155\n```\n\nNow, we add the two results together:\n```\n  35\n+7608\n-----\n8181\n```\n\nTherefore, the product of 15 and 02 is 9593. <|User|>Can you also show me how to solve this using the standard algorithm for multiplication, but this time starting with