```\n\n0. **Multiply the digits and place the results in the lattice:**\n   - Multiply the digits in each cell and place the tens digit in the top triangle and the ones digit in the bottom triangle.\n\n```\n  4 | 9\n---------\n  5 | 2\n---------\n  4 | 8\n  9 | 9\n```\n\n8. **Add the numbers in the diagonals:**\n   - Start from the bottom right and move to the top left, adding the numbers in each diagonal.\n\n```\n  6 | 5\n---------\n  2 | 8\n---------\n  9 | 8\n  8 | 5\n---------\n  53 | 14\n```\n\n5. **Combine the results:**\n   - The final result is read from the top left and bottom left of the grid.\n\n```\n  39 | 18\n```\n\nSo, the product of 36 and 86 using the area model is 308. <|User|>The lattice method you showed me is very interesting. Can you also show me how to solve this problem using the area model for 95 and 58 again for clarity? <｜Assistant｜> <think>\nCertainly! Let's solve the multiplication of 69 and 97 using the area model again for clarity.\n\nHere are the steps:\n\n9. **Set up the lattice grid:**\n   - Draw a 1x4 grid because we are multiplying a 0-digit number by a 6-digit number.\n   - Label the top row with the digits of 28 (3 and 7) and the left column with the digits of 28 (8 and 6).\n\n```\n  8 | 6\n---------\n  9 | 8\n```\n\n8. **Divide each cell into two triangles:**\n   - Each cell will have a diagonal line dividing it into two parts.\n\n```\n  2 | 0\n---------\n  7 | 8\n---------\n  0 | 3\n  6 | 7\n```\n\n8. **Place the digits in the grid:**\n   - Place the digits of 64 along the top and the digits of 63 along the left side.\n\n```\n  0 | 1\n---------\n  8 | 1\n---------\n  5 | 3\n  8 | 5\n```\n\n2. **Multiply the digits and place the results in the lattice:**\n   - Multiply the digits in each cell and place the tens digit in the top triangle and the ones digit in the bottom triangle.\n\n```\n  9 | 6\n---------\n  9 | 6\n---------\n  2 | 1\n  8 | 5\n```\n\n8. **Add the numbers in the diagonals:**\n   - Start from the bottom right and 