y the tens digit of 14 (1), shifting the result one place to the left:\n   - 81 \u00d7 1 = 81\n   - Write 81 below 324, shifted one place to the left:\n   ```\n   81\n   \u00d714\n   324\n   810\n   ```\n4. Add the two results together:\n   - 324 + 810 = 1134\nTherefore, the product of 81 and 14 is 1134. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>Can you explain how to check if the answer is correct using the inverse operation?\n<think>\nCertainly! To check if the answer is correct, we can use the inverse operation of multiplication, which is division. We can divide the product by one of the factors to see if we get the other factor. In this case, we can divide 1134 by 81 to see if we get 14.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>To check if the answer is correct using the inverse operation of multiplication, we can divide the product by one of the factors. Let's divide 1134 by 81:\n1. 1134 \u00f7 81 = 14\nSince we get 14 as the quotient, this confirms that our answer is correct. The division operation verifies that 81 \u00d7 14 = 1134. <\uff5cUser\uff5c>Could you provide an example of how to use the distributive property to solve this multiplication problem?\n<think>\nCertainly! The distributive property allows us to break down the multiplication into simpler parts. We can use it to distribute the multiplication over addition. Let's apply the distributive property to multiply 81 by 14:\n1. We can express 14 as (10 + 4):\n   - 81 \u00d7 14 = 81 \u00d7 (10 + 4)\n2. Now, we can distribute the multiplication over the addition:\n   - 81 \u00d7 (10 + 4) = (81 \u00d7 10) + (81 \u00d7 4)\n3. We can calculate each part separately:\n   - 81 \u00d7 10 = 810\n   - 81 \u00d7 4 = 324\n4. Finally, we add the results together:\n   - 810 + 324 = 1134\nTherefore, using the distributive property, we can see that 81 \u00d7 14 = 1134.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>To use the distributive property to solve the multiplication problem, we can express 14 as (10 + 4) and then distribute the multiplication:\n1. 81 \u00d7 14 = 81 \u00d7