      "text": "4536.\n</\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>\n<think>\nTo solve the problem of finding the product of 24 and 42, let's break it down step by step:\n\n1. First, we can use the standard multiplication method:\n   - Multiply 42 by 4 (the tens digit of 24), which gives us 168.\n   - Multiply 42 by 2 (the ones digit of 24), which gives us 84.\n   - Now, we add these two results together: 168 + 84 = 252.\n\n2. Alternatively, we can use the distributive property of multiplication over addition:\n   - We can express 24 as (20 + 4).\n   - Then, we can use the distributive property: 24 \u00d7 42 = (20 + 4) \u00d7 42 = 20 \u00d7 42 + 4 \u00d7 42.\n   - We already know that 20 \u00d7 42 = 840.\n   - And 4 \u00d7 42 = 168.\n   - Adding these two results together: 840 + 168 = 1008.\n\n3. Another method is to use the fact that 24 and 42 are both multiples of 6:\n   - 24 = 6 \u00d7 4\n   - 42 = 6 \u00d7 7\n   - Therefore, 24 \u00d7 42 = (6 \u00d7 4) \u00d7 (6 \u00d7 7) = 6 \u00d7 6 \u00d7 4 \u00d7 7 = 36 \u00d7 28.\n   - Now, we can break down 28 into 20 + 8:\n   - 36 \u00d7 28 = 36 \u00d7 (20 + 8) = 36 \u00d7 20 + 36 \u00d7 8.\n   - 36 \u00d7 20 = 720.\n   - 36 \u00d7 8 = 288.\n   - Adding these two results together: 720 + 288 = 1008.\n\nIn all these methods, we arrive at the same result. Therefore, the product of 24 and 42 is 1008.\n</think>\n<answer>\nThe product of 24 and 42 is 1008.\n</answer>",
