      "text": "4080.\n</\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>\n<answer>\nThe product of 77 and 66 is 4922.\n</answer>\n<think>\nTo solve the problem of finding the product of 77 and 66, I will follow these steps:\n1. First, I'll break down the multiplication into simpler parts. I can think of 77 as 70 + 7 and 66 as 60 + 6.\n2. Then, I'll use the distributive property of multiplication over addition to expand the expression:\n   (70 + 7) \u00d7 (60 + 6) = 70 \u00d7 60 + 70 \u00d7 6 + 7 \u00d7 60 + 7 \u00d7 6\n3. Now, I'll calculate each of these products separately:\n   70 \u00d7 60 = 4200\n   70 \u00d7 6 = 420\n   7 \u00d7 60 = 420\n   7 \u00d7 6 = 42\n4. Finally, I'll add all these products together:\n   4200 + 420 + 420 + 42 = 4922\nTherefore, the product of 77 and 66 is 4922.\n</think>\n<answer>\nThe product of 77 and 66 is 4922.\n</answer>",
